    "standardized_narrative": "In 2017, Syndicate 623 reported a prior year reserve release of $39.7 million, representing 5.82% of its opening gross claims outstanding. This was primarily attributed to a consistent reserving philosophy that allows for the release of risk margins as uncertainty reduces, and generally favorable claims development, particularly benign claims experience in Specialty lines for the 2010, 2013, 2014, and 2015 years of account. While there were mentions of negative developments on prior year risks in the Political, accident & contingency division, the overall movement was a net release across the portfolio.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "consistent reserving philosophy, with initial reserves being set to include risk margins that may be released over time as and when any uncertainty reduces",
      "The margin held above the actuarial estimate was 5% at the end of 2017 (2016: 6.6%). This margin decreased in 2017 which was in part due to the catastrophe activity in the second half of the year, which resulted in much lower margins than usual in the affected areas.",
      "negative developments on risks from prior years",
      "relatively benign claims experience",
      "more difficult years, from a claims perspective, immediately following the 2008 credit crunch are now well behind us."
